Article 4 (Processing of Unique Identifying Information, etc.)
Where unavoidable for performing any of the following duties, the head of a relevant institution may process materials containing sensitive information under Article 23 of the Personal Information Protection Act, and resident registration numbers, passport numbers and foreigner registration numbers under subparagraphs 1, 2 and 4 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act:
1. Duties concerning the reporting, handling, etc. of improper solicitations and money, goods, etc. prohibited from receipt under Articles 7 and 9 of the Act;
2. Duties concerning the reporting, handling, etc. of outside lectures, etc. under Article 10 of the Act;
3. Duties concerning the reporting, handling, etc. of violations of the Act under Articles 13 and 14 of the Act;
4. Duties concerning the protection and compensation of reporting persons, etc. under Article 15 of the Act;
5. Duties concerning recovery of unjust enrichment under Article 17 of the Act.
